# SPACBR — AUR packages
#
# Per §41-43 of CLAUDE.md: only add an entry when a specific, justified
# need can't be met officially, and note that justification next to
# it. The installer needs exactly one AUR helper (paru) to build these
# — don't add a second.
#
# arc-gtk-theme was dropped (previously the only entry here). Verified
# for real on a machine with no AUR helper: gtk-2.0/3.0/4.0 configs and
# xinitrc's GTK_THEME all assumed Arc-Dark, it silently failed to load
# since it was never installed, and every GTK app (PCManFM, Zathura,
# GTK dialogs) fell back to plain light GTK -- completely defeating the
# unified dark visual identity §34 requires. It was also AUR-only, last
# updated 2025-03-31, and flagged out-of-date since 2025-11-30 with no
# maintainer response -- a real §42 "avoid abandoned packages" risk on
# top of the AUR-helper fragility. Replaced with GTK's own bundled
# Adwaita dark variant (gtk-theme-name=Adwaita + prefer-dark-theme=1 +
# GTK_THEME="Adwaita:dark" in xinitrc) -- ships with the gtk3/gtk4
# packages themselves, so it can never be silently missing, needs no
# AUR helper, and is maintained upstream by GTK itself. This file has
# no entries as a result; keep it that way unless a specific need
# genuinely can't be met officially (§41).

